<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eritrea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eritrea is a country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>'s port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adulis">Adulis</a> lay there, and from the late nineteenth century it became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s first colony and a base for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. It gained independence in 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eritrea.jpg" alt="Eritrea" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Eritrea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Aksumite Empire emerged in the highlands of northern Ethiopia and <b>Eritrea</b> around the first century CE, though its roots extend to the pre-Aksumite civilisation that had absorbed South Arabian cultural and linguistic influences centuries earlier.</blockquote><a href="/empire/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The famine of 1983–85 was under way, as Alex de Waal observed, months before the drought; the government deliberately multiplied its effects in Tigray and <b>Eritrea</b>, channelling aid through companies close to the Derg, and about 1.2 million people died, most in present-day Tigray and Amhara.</blockquote><a href="/empire/derg">Derg · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Together with Massawa, occupied in 1885, this grew into the colony of <b>Eritrea</b>, formally proclaimed in 1890, and was followed by the gradual establishment of Italian Somaliland on the Horn of Africa.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Colonial expansion followed, with <b>Eritrea</b> organised as a colony in 1890 and a protectorate over much of Somalia, but the attempt to conquer Ethiopia ended in defeat at the Battle of Adwa in 1896.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Egyptians traded with Lebanon for cedar and sailed the length of the Red Sea to the Kingdom of Punt, in modern <b>Eritrea</b>, for ebony, ivory and aromatic resins; Sahure of the Fifth Dynasty commanded an expedition there.</blockquote><a href="/empire/old-kingdom-of-egypt">Old Kingdom of Egypt · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The settlement of its borders, with Oman in 1992, with Saudi Arabia by the Treaty of Jeddah in 2000 and with <b>Eritrea</b> after arbitration over the Hanish Islands in 1998–1999, ended long-running disputes.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Republic of Yemen · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
